WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.200
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:34.820
The Arrow of Sagittarius

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.420
Hey, is that the air raid siren?!

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.340
The men on watch must be dreaming!

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.340
They must've mistaken one of our own for the enemy's.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.090
It's going to be warm today.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.260
What's the matter? You got malaria or something?

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.810
No. The resident mouse isn't coming out.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.730
He comes out for food every morning.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.810
Hey mousey!

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.810
What's the matter? Where are you?

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.250
Cease Fire! Alpha Strike! Commence Attack!

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.550
Okay! Alpha Strike, phase one.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.890
Get down!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.310
Hurry! It's for real!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.640
Run for the jungle!

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.110
Get back to your units!

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.820
Leader! We haven't had breakfast yet!

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.650
You fool! How will you eat breakfast if you're dead?!

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.660
The villagers and the mice knew this would happen!

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.450
W-Where are these planes coming from?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.790
F-From the sea?!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.010
Sir! The first unit will be ashore in 15 minutes.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.810
The second unit will be onshore by 8:15.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.020
We're really proceeding as planned?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.230
Yes. But we did experience some difficulty...

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.860
...getting the equipment on shore.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.150
Why haven't the Japanese fired at us yet?

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.820
Either they have something up their sleeves...

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.620
...or they're nothing but a bunch of fools.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.020
I will go ashore too.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.940
We'll need to take the bridgehead at the red beach.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.060
Sir, the area hasn't been secured.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.940
Please wait a little longer.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.490
Our objective isn't just to land.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.490
It's to occupy the airstrip!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.620
Keep your heads down!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.040
The bomb shrapnel could slice off your head!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.800
If the bombs fall into the trenches...

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.670
...we'll be blown to smithereens. Reduced to ashes!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.760
At the rate they're firing...

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.720
...even the island's going to change shape.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:48.970
XO!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.770
You're sure we can trust Lieutenant Kusaka, right?

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.350
If the Lieutenant's strategy comes through...

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.020
...the Japanese Army should retreat and give up the island.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.610
When that happens, there'll be no need for us to take action.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.150
And this operation will be stopped, right?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.400
If the Japanese Army decides to pull out...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.240
...the 8th Division will not send its troops here.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.830
And the First Battle of Solomon will not take place!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.460
We'll only need to lead this unit to safety.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.460
And we can all get outta here.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.670
What if the 8th Division arrives?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.130
What'll happen then?

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.090
Then either the Lieutenant couldn't convince the Admiral...

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.260
...or we've all been had by him.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:33.390
We'd then have to drive the 11,000 Marines from this island.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.390
We're the only ones who can.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.400
Am I right, Yosuke?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.020
We'll just proceed as planned.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.650
You're talking too much, Kohei.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.190
If I stop talking, my thoughts will start to run wild!

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.160
Trapped between life and death, relying only on intuition and luck.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.120
So this is the battlefield?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.120
How much damage have we sustained?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.620
The main ship has slight damage.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.500
We've lost 11 support aircrafts.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.460
And Fletcher has pulled out.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.130
The second unit has landed successfully.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.220
Expansion of the bridgehead is in progress.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.760
No large-scale resistance from the Japanese yet.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:19.690
It isn't just the Japanese we're up against.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.820
Complex terrain aside, this island has a dense jungle.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.910
Damn it.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.870
It's so dark even in the afternoon.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.800
The US Marines' landing on Guadalcanal.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.470
The Shoe String Operation.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.760
Even after the Rabaul Air Squadron assault...

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.430
...more than half the Marines have gone ashore.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.390
It's just like history.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.230
Lieutenant.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:05.070
How is he? How is Lieutenant Tsuda doing?

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.820
Sir, he hasn't stepped out of his room.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.090
Lieutenant Kusaka took every opportunity to explore this ship.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.260
But you seem to feel otherwise.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.590
I am very different from Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.180
I could never match up to him.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.180
What's the difference?

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.060
The power that comes from knowing the future.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.230
I don't think I have the strength to bear that burden.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.900
You seem to know something as well.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.450
Right before he left for Truk...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.290
...the Lieutenant told you something, didn't he?

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.790
Members of this ship have gone ashore to Guadalcanal!

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.000
If there's a change in the situation...

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.960
I must let them know as soon as possible!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.970
What is Kusaka planning?!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.010
Answer me, Lieutenant Tsuda!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.720
Target spotted!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.470
30 miles northwest of Savo Island!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.060
Entering in single file formation!

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.440
Fleet speed, 26 knots!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.230
T-This is?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.810
8 ships verified! It's the 8th Division...

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.900
...coming from Rabaul!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.500
Lieutenant!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.510
It's the 8th Division!

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.850
From: the 8th Division Fleet.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.140
To: Military Headquarters and Commander-in-Chief.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.520
We are currently heading north from the Bouganville Straits.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.570
We're sailing at high speed...

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.530
...through Isabella and New Georgia Islands.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.360
Upon arrival at Guadalcanal...

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.450
We will launch an immediate attack.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.410
Followed by a speedy retreat.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.660
All units stand by!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.250
All units stand by! All ships clear!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.760
Watch report!

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.390
Starboard 30 degrees, heavy enemy cruiser sighted!

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:43.350
Seaplane to drop off illuminator!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.140
All ships prepare to attack!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.140
All cannons ready!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.240
Alert!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.740
Unidentified planes and vessels sighted!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.240
Head vessel, heavy cruiser Canberra, distance 3700.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.200
Starboard torpedoes, fire!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.880
An attack! All hands, battle alert!

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.800
Head vessel has taken two hits!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.430
Main cannons! Fire!

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.400
Rear vessels have been hit too!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.610
Enemy spotted at 10 o'clock!

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.610
There's four, no, five vessels!

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.530
Turn on the spotlights!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.760
Commander, it's a clean hit.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.550
Admiral Yamamoto will be pleased to hear about this.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.100
What is that?!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.940
The ship's engulfed in flames!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.820
It's an enemy assault! Will they be alright?

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.860
The Patrol Unit has been attacked by the enemy!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.530
They're engaged in battle now!

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.830
Details on the enemy vessels?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.290
According to the reports...

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:30.120
4 heavy cruisers, no light cruisers, and 3 to 4 destroyers.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.130
Due to the chaotic situation, no further information is available!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:39.880
Contact British Admirals Crutchley and Turner of the escort.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.720
Yes, Sir!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.390
The enemy isn't targeting the patrol fleet.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.310
It's this convoy ship they want.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.650
Due to the delay in docking...

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:56.020
...the convoy is still loaded with food and ammunition.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.280
If this ship is sunk...

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:02.740
The men on shore will be left stranded in enemy territory.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.200
Sea battle confirmed, north of Guadalcanal.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:12.580
It seems that the Allied Fleet has been badly hit by the 8th Division.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.130
So this is the answer. History is unchanged.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.210
The Japanese Navy will not give up Guadalcanal Island.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.720
And neither will Kusaka!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.890
How dare he lie about stopping the Guadalcanal Operation.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.810
No, it's changing already.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.520
Lieutenant Kusaka is making his move.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.070
Yosuke! In the end, Kusaka's still an Imperial Navy Soldier.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.820
Do not trust him!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.410
We'll commence with our own operation!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.210
Everyone here is fine.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.630
But my ears are still ringing from those bombs.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.420
Right now, we've arrived at Red Beach.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.630
Where the US Marines have also landed.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.300
What's most important now, is the 8th Division's next move.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.850
What if Kusaka intended to capture this area?

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:12.470
The 8th Division took out the Allied patrolling fleet...

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.810
...in just 35 minutes.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:20.150
But historically, Admiral Mikawa was wary of the carriers...

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.900
...pulls out without launching any further attacks.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.870
If he knows that there aren't any carriers around...

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.450
...he will proceed to attack the convoy ships.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.080
According to history...

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.960
...after the close encounter with the 8th Division,

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.580
...the US Convoy ships will abandon their marines.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.920
And pull out of this area by afternoon.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:43.800
But, we can't let them leave empty-handed.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:47.260
Both Vandegrift and his unit must stay on board.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.760
Let's focus on this objective.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.100
Once the 8th Division pulls out without a second assault.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.980
We will begin our operation.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.270
That's right. Execution time, 0300.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.610
We must destroy the US Marines' morale!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.570
We can put this to good use now.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.360
Get as close as possible to the enemy camp.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.120
Our target is the supplies they have piled on the beach!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.120
Damage report!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.630
The map room, Commander's quarters.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.750
And the 2nd High Angle Gun Room have all been hit.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:26.760
The fires have been mostly extinguished.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.720
Navigation and Battle Status unaffected!

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.140
All our maps have been blown away.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.680
What? Do we know our way home at least?

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:37.940
Well done.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.150
4 heavy cruisers sunk.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:43.020
Two destroyers down. Minimal damage on our side.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.190
Commander, it's a major victory!

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:48.400
Now, the targeted US Convoy ships...

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.780
...are completely naked!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.160
Let's go in and get 'em!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.410
There may be carriers around, but they won't be a problem.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.410
No, there aren't any carriers.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.370
Or any more enemy attacks.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.170
What?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.130
Shall we proceed, then?

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.050
Everyone, you've all done a good job.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.380
Our mission is completed.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.390
All ships regroup!

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.350
We will turn back now!

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.390
Hard to port!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.310
Look out for any sign of enemy activity.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.360
Reinforce the patrols.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.940
All ships back to single-file formation!

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:32.030
The 8th Division is heading northwest.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.620
They're pulling out.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.240
Just like in history, they didn't take out the convoy ships.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.000
This is the first step to Japan's defeat at Guadalcanal.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.130
So Lieutenant Kusaka didn't tell Headquarters any of this?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.960
Either that, or what he said was disregarded.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.760
Arrow, Fortune Inspector. Do you copy?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.090
Could you skip the formal terminology?

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.390
The 8th Division has left this area.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:00.930
Operation Sagittarius will commence at 0300.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.770
Arrow. Roger.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.480
The Operation is going as planned.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:12.570
Commander, the rest is up to you.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:18.080
Canberra, Quincy and the Vincennes have been sunk!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.870
Astoria and Chicago are badly damaged and immobile.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.580
Orders given to abandon ship!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.500
Where's the Japanese fleet now?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.170
Sir! At 0200, they headed northwest...

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.130
...and pulled out of the area.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.590
They pulled out?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.180
A total defeat.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.470
That Oriental Island...

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.430
...may be lacking in natural resources...

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.480
...but their skill and technology more than compensates for that.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.480
Looks like they really are formidable.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.150
My Eastern Fleet in the Indian Ocean...

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.280
...was taken out by their skilled Zero Fighters.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.530
One of my submarines also submitted a report...

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.990
...saying they had sonar equipped homing torpedoes.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.450
Sonar equipped torpedoes?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.250
That's just the illusion of a defeated soldier.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.670
Stories like that aren't uncommon on the battlefield.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.920
It's evidence that fear of the Japanese...

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.880
...is spreading through the army.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.970
I prefer red tea.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.090
We don't have time to waste.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.970
The Japanese's retreat is a blessing.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.180
We need to pull out our troops right now!

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.930
Arrogance and optimism aside.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.810
Too much caution could easily become a disadvantage.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.520
Two things are crucial on the battlefield...

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.400
...composure, and military logistics.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:37.910
As vanguard of the Allied Forces, the First Division Fleet...

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.830
...will not pull out until we have captured Guadalcanal Island.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.870
I don't care if the Navy wants to retreat.

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.460
But I want those supplies delivered on shore...

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.420
No matter the cost!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.420
Of course.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.090
I will do my best to deliver them by morning.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.380
This is no blessing.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.800
The Japanese Fleet only retreated to avoid damaging...

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.220
...the ships given to them by the Emperor.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.270
They still haven't recovered from their defeat at Midway.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.480
They're just as frightened as we are.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:12.230
Food and water rations.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.360
Medical supplies.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.490
Ammunition.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:20.160
That's enough for 11 thousand Marines...

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.120
...to last a week of fighting.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.830
Commander, what's our target?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.250
The food rations.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.870
They've got a mountain load.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.130
Over there.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.500
Is that flour?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.050
Shouldn't we be going after ammunitions?

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.880
If we blow up their ammunition...

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:39.890
We'll definitely put a damper on their morale.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:43.600
And the US Convoy will be able to watch the fireworks too.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.060
For the sake of the operations later...

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.600
I think its more important that we destroy their morale.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.360
Oguri, can you imagine how many soldiers would be killed...

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.070
...by that kind of explosion?

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.230
But then, that ammunition will be used...

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.070
...for killing Japanese instead!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.610
Listen.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.530
If our objective was to kill, we wouldn't be here at all.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.580
Operation Sagittarius...

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.500
...aims at intimidation, not aggression.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.920
But what happens if they refuse to be intimidated?

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.500
The Americans are terrified of unseen enemies in the jungle.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.630
Just like in Vietnam.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:19.880
But, be they Japanese or American...

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.840
...the dead cannot be brought back to life.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:25.260
Don't you forget that.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:28.560
It's time.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.140
Petty Officer Enomoto! Prepare the laser now.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.150
Yes!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.650
Fortune Inspector, Arrow.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.570
Operation Sagittarius ready to commence!

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:38.940
Roger!

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.150
Commence Operation!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.160
General! I've received a strange message.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.450
Is it from the Japanese?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.450
I thought so but, it's addressed to you.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.960
Addressed to me? What's it say?

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.040
It says...

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.380
A warning to Major General Vandegrift.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.210
At 3 this morning...

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.010
We will be launching an attack on the landed supplies.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.510
We will be using a mi... missile?

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:05.640
It's a weapon that far surpasses the technology of this era.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.600
Before we take the lives of your officers...

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:12.980
...we will take the bread and pancakes from your breakfast.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.400
This is a firm request, I repeat, a firm request.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:19.820
And a demonstration requiring the removal of US troops.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:23.030
The operation is called Sagittarius.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.040
Sagittarius, the zodiac sign.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.870
A fancy person, uncharacteristic of the Japanese.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.670
It seems they're targeting the flour.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.840
It's a bluff. It's a confusion tactic.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.970
He's telling us to switch to rice instead?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.090
Get me some coffee please.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.430
We do have some on shore right?

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.390
Yes sir!

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:54.020
This operation was supposed to be classified.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.900
How did they know it was my division on shore?

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.150
Data for Red Beach, Northern Guadalcanal.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.490
Re-entered into Inertia Navigation System!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.240
Final navigation set to laser guidance mode!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.580
Harpoon! Ready to fire!

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.460
The Guadalcanal Battle is following history.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.710
Our appearance may not have had...

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.340
...such a big impact on the course of history.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.760
This next shot, however...

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.640
...is certainly going to make an impact.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.350
We're about to radically alter the present...

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.190
...and the history of the world we came from.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.900
I wonder how future historians will record this change...

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.120
...with a weapon that's not supposed to exist.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.580
0255

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.580
Captain, it's time.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:54.960
Begin Attack!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.170
Commence attack now!

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:03.710
The Sagittarius Arrow has been fired!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.200
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.440
Just peacefully

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:34.220
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:47.130
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.730
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:59.810
I kept on praying

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:11.650
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:27.340
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:42.100
Fortune Inspector, Arrow.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:44.220
Captain, I need to speak with you.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:46.270
Appearance of a fleet not recorded in history?

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.270
What's going on here?!

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:50.980
Unfortunately, we're in the midst of war.

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.440
Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:56.740
Can you swear on your life, can you swear to God.

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:58.780
That you've chosen the right path?

00:23:58.990 --> 00:24:01.700
Commander Kadomatsu, I hope you can hear my voice.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:04.950
Next Episode: The Land of Gold

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:04.120
I don't want you to die!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
